<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a bug in the `parse_atxheader` function in `src/document.c`.

When parsing an ATX-style header (e.g., `### Header`), the function `parse_atxheader` is called. If the header has no content (e.g., `#######`), the code at `src/document.c:2740` is executed. This line calls the `header` callback with `NULL` for the `content` and `attr` arguments: `doc->md.header(ob, NULL, NULL, (int)level, &doc->data);`.

In this specific crash, the `header` callback is `toc_header` (from `hoedown_html_toc_renderer_new`). The `toc_header` function in `src/html.c` does not handle the case where the `content` argument is `NULL`. It attempts to dereference the `NULL` pointer at line 987: `rndr_header_id(ob, content->data, content->size, 1, data);`, causing a segmentation fault.

The fix should be in `toc_header` to add a null check for the `content` parameter before dereferencing it. For example:

```c
if (content) {
rndr_header_id(ob, content->data, content->size, 1, data);
}
```

This will prevent the crash when an empty header is parsed.
</crash-analysis>

